msgctxt "NonParametricSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"This analysis computes a survival curve for censored data using the Kaplan-"
"Meier estimator for single-event survival data. It estimates the probability "
"of survival over time, allowing you to understand and visualize the "
"distribution of survival times within your data. The analysis accommodates "
"censored observations (subjects for whom the event has not occurred during "
"the study period) and enables comparison of survival curves across different "
"groups using statistical tests such as the Log-Rank test, Peto and Peto "
"test, and Fleming-Harrington test. Additionally, you can generate life "
"tables to summarize survival data at specified intervals."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "NonParametricSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid "Time to Event"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "NonParametricSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Select the variable that represents the time until the event or censoring "
"occurs."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "NonParametricSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid "Event Status"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "NonParametricSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Choose the variable that indicates the event status, specifying whether each "
"observation is an event or censored."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "NonParametricSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid "Event Indicator"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "NonParametricSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Specify the value in the Event Status variable that indicates the occurrence "
"of the event."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "NonParametricSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid "Strata"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "NonParametricSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Select variables to define strata, allowing separate survival curves for "
"each stratum."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "NonParametricSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid "Weights"
msgstr "Ponderaciones"

msgctxt "NonParametricSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Select a variable for case weights, weighting each observation accordingly "
"in the model."
msgstr ""
"Seleccionar una variable para las ponderaciones de los casos, ponderando "
"cada observación como corresponde en el modelo."

msgctxt "NonParametricSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid "Censoring summary"
msgstr "Resumen de censura"

msgctxt "NonParametricSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Create a summary table with information about the censoring status of the "
"data."
msgstr ""
"Generar una tabla resumen con información sobre el estado de censura en los "
"datos."

msgctxt "NonParametricSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid "Tests"
msgstr "Contrastes"

msgctxt "NonParametricSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid "Log-rank (Mantel-Haenszel)"
msgstr "Log-rango (Mantel-Haenszel)"

msgctxt "NonParametricSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Include the Log-Rank (Mantel-Haenszel) test to compare survival curves "
"across strata."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "NonParametricSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid "Peto and Peto"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "NonParametricSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Include the Peto and Peto modification of the Gehan-Wilcoxon test to compare "
"survival curves across strata."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "NonParametricSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid "Flemming-Harrington"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "NonParametricSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Include the Fleming-Harrington test to compare survival curves across "
"strata., with a customizable rho parameter."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "NonParametricSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid "Rho"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "NonParametricSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Set the rho parameter for the Fleming-Harrington test, controlling the "
"weight given to different time points (values between 0 and 1)."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "NonParametricSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid "Life table"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "NonParametricSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Generate a life table summarizing survival data at specified time intervals."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "NonParametricSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid "Steps type"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "NonParametricSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Select the method to define intervals for the life table: Default, "
"Quantiles, or Fixed size. Quantiles uses empirical quantiles of the observed "
"times, including censored times, after frequency weights are applied; these "
"are not quantiles of the estimated survival distribution."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "NonParametricSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid "Default"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "NonParametricSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid "Quantiles"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "NonParametricSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid "Fixed size"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "NonParametricSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid "Number"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "NonParametricSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid "Specify the number of intervals when using Quantiles as the steps type."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "NonParametricSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid "Round steps"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "NonParametricSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Round the interval boundaries to the nearest integer when using Quantiles "
"steps."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "NonParametricSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid "From"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "NonParametricSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid "Set the starting time for intervals when using Fixed size steps."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "NonParametricSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid "Size"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "NonParametricSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid "Define the size of each interval when using Fixed size steps."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "NonParametricSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid "To"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "NonParametricSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid "Set the ending time for intervals when using Fixed size steps."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricMixtureSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"This analysis models survival times as a finite mixture of components from "
"the same parametric family. Constrained maximum likelihood imposes the "
"specified minimum standard deviation of log survival time in every "
"component. Several starting values, each refined by EM iterations, are used; "
"the converged solution with the highest likelihood satisfying the bound is "
"reported."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricMixtureSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"This analysis performs a parametric mixture survival analysis. The survival "
"times are modeled as a finite mixture of components from the same parametric "
"family. The likelihood is maximized directly from several starting values "
"(each refined by a few EM iterations). The non-degenerate solution with the "
"highest likelihood is reported. If all solutions are degenerate, the best of "
"them is reported with a warning."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricMixtureSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid "Interval Start"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricMixtureSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Select the variable that represents the start time of the observation "
"interval. Only available when Censoring Type is set to Interval or Counting."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricMixtureSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid "Interval End"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricMixtureSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Select the variable that represents the end time of the observation "
"interval. Only available when Censoring Type is set to Interval or Counting."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricMixtureSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid "Time to Event"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricMixtureSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Select the variable that represents the time until the event or censoring "
"occurs. Only available when Censoring Type is set to Right."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricMixtureSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid "Event Status"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricMixtureSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Choose the variable that indicates the event status, specifying whether each "
"observation is an event or censored."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricMixtureSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid "Event Indicator"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricMixtureSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Specify the value in the Event Status variable that indicates the occurrence "
"of the event."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricMixtureSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid "Covariates"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricMixtureSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Add continuous variables as covariates to include them in the mixture model. "
"The covariates affect the location parameter of each component with separate "
"coefficients."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricMixtureSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid "Factors"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricMixtureSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Add categorical variables as factors to include them in the mixture model. "
"The factors affect the location parameter of each component with separate "
"coefficients."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricMixtureSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid "Weights"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricMixtureSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Select a variable for case weights, weighting each observation accordingly "
"in the model."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricMixtureSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid "Subgroup"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricMixtureSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Select a variable for subgroup analysis, allowing for separate analyses "
"within each subgroup."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricMixtureSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid "Censoring Type"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricMixtureSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Select right-censored data, counting-process data with entry and exit times, "
"or interval-censored data (including left-censored observations)."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricMixtureSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid "Right"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricMixtureSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid "Counting"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricMixtureSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid "Interval"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricMixtureSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"If interval censoring is selected, the following coding needs to be used: "
"left-censored data is represented as (NA, t2), right-censored data as (t1, "
"NA), exact data as (t, t), and interval-censored data as (t1, t2)."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricMixtureSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid "Censoring summary"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricMixtureSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Create a summary table with information about the censoring status of the "
"data."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricMixtureSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid "Distribution"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricMixtureSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Choose the parametric distribution of the mixture components (all components "
"come from the same distribution). All fits and display results for all "
"'Selected parametric families' in the 'Advanced' section. 'Best AIC' and "
"'Best BIC' fit all `Selected parametric families` in the Advanced section "
"and display the results only for a parametric family with the lowest AIC/"
"BIC. Families without a closed-form weighted fit (gamma, Gompertz, and the "
"generalized families) are considerably slower to estimate."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricMixtureSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid "Exponential"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricMixtureSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid "Gamma"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricMixtureSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid "Generalized F"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricMixtureSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid "Generalized gamma"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricMixtureSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid "Gompertz"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricMixtureSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid "Log-logistic"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricMixtureSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid "Log-normal"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricMixtureSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid "Weibull"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricMixtureSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid "Generalized gamma (original)"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricMixtureSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid "Generalized F (original)"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricMixtureSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid "All"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricMixtureSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid "Best AIC"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricMixtureSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid "Best BIC"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricMixtureSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid "Components"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricMixtureSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Choose the number of mixture components. 'All' fits and displays results for "
"one up to the maximum number of components set in the 'Advanced' section. "
"'Best AIC' and 'Best BIC' fit the same models and display the results only "
"for the number of components with the lowest AIC/BIC. A fixed number of "
"components is not limited by the maximum number of components."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricMixtureSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid "Model"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricMixtureSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid "Interpret model"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricMixtureSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Select the model to interpret. Defaults to the last specified model. "
"Alternatives are 'All' which produces results for all of the specified "
"models or 'Best' which produces results for the best fitting model based on "
"either AIC or BIC. The selection proceeds within each subgroup from the "
"distribution to the number of components to the model: 'Best' keeps the "
"level of the best fitting model across all remaining distributions, numbers "
"of components, and models, and 'All' selects separately within each of its "
"levels (e.g., all distributions with the best number of components and the "
"best model within each distribution)."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricMixtureSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Include a table with information about the model fit. The BIC uses the "
"number of observations (including censored observations and weighted by the "
"case weights) as the sample size."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricMixtureSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid "Mixture"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricMixtureSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid "Mean and median"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricMixtureSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Include a table with the mean and the median lifetime of each mixture "
"component. They correspond to the reference level of factors and zero value "
"of covariates. The mixing probabilities and the parameters of the components "
"are reported in the coefficients summary. Components are ordered by their "
"median lifetime."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricMixtureSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid "Classification"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricMixtureSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Include a table with the number and proportion of observations assigned to "
"each component based on their highest posterior probability, the mean "
"posterior probability of the assigned observations, and the relative entropy "
"of the classification."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricMixtureSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Select the quantiles at which survival times are predicted: evenly spaced "
"Quantiles, a Sequence, or Custom probabilities."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricMixtureSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Specify the number of quantiles of the predicted survival when using "
"Quantiles as the steps type."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricMixtureSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Select the time points for prediction tables: Equal spacing, a Sequence, or "
"Custom times. Time plots place unrounded points adaptively within the "
"selected range."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricMixtureSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Define the time increment when using Sequence steps. Leaving this blank uses "
"one tenth of the selected time range."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricMixtureSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid "Specify custom time points for predictions."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricMixtureSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid "Merge plots across components"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricMixtureSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Merge the plots for survival time across the numbers of components into a "
"single plot. Only available when all numbers of components are displayed and "
"no model selection is being performed."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricMixtureSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Merge the plots for survival probabilities, hazard, cumulative hazard, and "
"restricted mean survival across the numbers of components into a single "
"plot. Only available when all numbers of components are displayed and no "
"model selection is being performed."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricMixtureSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid "Diagnostics"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricMixtureSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid "Residuals vs. predicted time"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricMixtureSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid "Estimation diagnostics"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricMixtureSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Include a table with the diagnostics of the estimation of each mixture "
"model: the number of starting values, how many of them reached the reported "
"solution, the log-likelihood of the reported and of the next best distinct "
"solution, the number of degenerate candidate solutions, the effective sample "
"size and the effective number of events of the smallest component, optimizer "
"convergence, and whether the Hessian of the likelihood is positive definite."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricMixtureSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid "Component plot"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricMixtureSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Include a plot with the fitted mixture and its components. The components "
"are evaluated at the same covariate values as the predictions."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricMixtureSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid "Type"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricMixtureSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Select the displayed function: the survival probability of the mixture and "
"of each component, the failure probability of the mixture and of each "
"component, the density of the mixture and the weighted density of each "
"component (which sum to the mixture density), or the hazard of the mixture "
"and of each component."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricMixtureSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid "Survival probability"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricMixtureSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid "Failure probability"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricMixtureSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid "Density"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricMixtureSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid "Hazard"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricMixtureSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid "Observed data"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricMixtureSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Overlay a histogram of the observed time distribution on the fitted "
"densities. For right-censored data, bin probabilities are estimated with "
"Kaplan-Meier and any unobserved tail probability is retained. The fitted "
"curves use the prediction covariate settings; the histogram describes the "
"full sample within each subgroup."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricMixtureSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Merge the probability plots across the numbers of components into a single "
"plot. Only available when all numbers of components are displayed and no "
"model selection is being performed."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricMixtureSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid "Advanced"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricMixtureSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid "Selected Parametric Distributions"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricMixtureSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid "Constrain minimum spread"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricMixtureSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Fit by constrained maximum likelihood with a minimum standard deviation of "
"the natural logarithm of survival time in every component, including one-"
"component models. Available for log-normal, Weibull, log-logistic, and gamma "
"distributions; other distributions are deselected. Checkbox choices made in "
"Selected Parametric Distributions before turning the constraint on are "
"restored when it is turned off again, provided the analysis form has not "
"been reloaded. When the bound is active, point estimates remain available "
"but standard errors, confidence intervals, covariance estimates, and regular "
"inferential tests are not reported."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricMixtureSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid "Relative"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricMixtureSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid "Absolute"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricMixtureSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Set the minimum log-time standard deviation relative to an unconstrained one-"
"component fit of the same distribution, or as an absolute value. The "
"reference fit uses the same data, predictors, censoring, and weights and is "
"computed separately for each model and subgroup."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricMixtureSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid "Minimum log-time SD"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricMixtureSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Set a positive percentage of the unconstrained one-component model's log-"
"time standard deviation as the minimum for every component. The default is "
"1%. For models with predictors, the reference is the conditional "
"distribution's log-time standard deviation. For delayed entry, it refers to "
"the distribution before conditioning on entry."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricMixtureSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Set a positive lower bound, up to 100, on the standard deviation of the "
"natural logarithm of survival time. Choose a minimum justified by the "
"application and check sensitivity to other values; 0.1 is an editable "
"preset, not a universal recommendation. The bound is unchanged when the "
"units of survival time change. For delayed entry, it bounds the component "
"distribution before conditioning on entry."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricMixtureSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid "Maximum components"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricMixtureSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Set the maximum number of components fitted when 'All', 'Best AIC', or 'Best "
"BIC' is selected as the number of components."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricMixtureSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid "Starting Values"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricMixtureSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Select the starting values of the constrained mixture estimation. The "
"converged solution with the highest likelihood satisfying the minimum "
"component spread is reported. More starting values reduce the risk of a "
"local optimum at a higher computational cost."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricMixtureSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Select the starting values of the mixture estimation. The likelihood is "
"maximized directly from every selected starting value and the non-degenerate "
"solution with the highest likelihood is reported. If all solutions are "
"degenerate, the best of them is reported with a warning. More starting "
"values make it more likely that the reported solution is the global maximum, "
"at a proportionally higher computational cost."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricMixtureSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid "K-means"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricMixtureSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Start from a k-means clustering of the log survival times. The likelihood is "
"maximized directly from this starting value."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricMixtureSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid "Quantiles"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricMixtureSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Start from partitions of the survival times by their quantiles: a partition "
"into groups of equal size and partitions that isolate the tails (the lowest "
"and the highest 15% for two components, 15/70/15% for three components, and "
"10/40/40/10% for four components). The likelihood is maximized directly from "
"each of these starting values."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricMixtureSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid "Split of the previous solution"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricMixtureSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Start from the solution with one component fewer, splitting each of its "
"components into a lower and an upper half. The likelihood is maximized "
"directly from each of these starting values. The solution with one component "
"fewer is estimated for this purpose when it is not part of the analysis."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricMixtureSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid "Random"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricMixtureSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Start from random centres drawn from the observed event times, assigning "
"each observation to the nearest centre. The likelihood is maximized directly "
"from each of these starting values. Random starting values are the main "
"protection against reporting a local optimum."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricMixtureSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid "Set the number of random starting values."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricMixtureSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid "EM iterations"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricMixtureSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Set the number of EM iterations that refine each starting value before the "
"likelihood is maximized directly. The state after the first and after the "
"last EM iteration are both used as starting values of the direct "
"maximization."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricMixtureSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid "Output Formatting"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricMixtureSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid "Include full dataset in subgroup analysis"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricMixtureSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Include the full dataset output in the subgroup analysis. This option is "
"only available when the subgroup analysis is selected."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricMixtureSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid "Compare models across distributions"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricMixtureSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Compare models across distributions. This option is only available when the "
"multiple models and parametric distributions are specified."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricMixtureSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid "Compare models across components"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricMixtureSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Compare models across the numbers of components. This option is only "
"available when multiple models and numbers of components are specified."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricMixtureSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid "Always display model information"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricMixtureSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Always display model information (distribution, number of components, and "
"model name) in output tables."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid "This analysis performs a parametric survival analysis."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid "Interval Start"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Select the variable that represents the start time of the observation "
"interval. Only available when Censoring Type is set to Interval or Counting."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid "Interval End"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Select the variable that represents the end time of the observation "
"interval. Only available when Censoring Type is set to Interval or Counting."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid "Time to Event"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Select the variable that represents the time until the event or censoring "
"occurs. Only available when Censoring Type is set to Right."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid "Event Status"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Choose the variable that indicates the event status, specifying whether each "
"observation is an event or censored."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid "Event Indicator"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Specify the value in the Event Status variable that indicates the occurrence "
"of the event."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid "Covariates"
msgstr "Covariables"

msgctxt "ParametricSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid ""
"Add continuous variables as covariates to include them in the parametric "
"survival model."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "ParametricSurvivalAnalysis|"
msgid "Factors"
msgstr "Factores"

msgctxt "ParametricSurvivalAnalysis|"
